\ arith.fam — the node's arithmetic (docs/NODE.md, step 1): the 32×32→64
\ product, BabyBear and its degree-4 extension, and wide integers.  RV32I
\ has no multiply, so the product is in software: by quarter squares over
\ 16-bit halves, uv = S[u+v] - S[|u-v|] with S[n] = floor(n^2/4) from a
\ table of 2^17 words (512 KiB) built once by arinit.
\
\ BabyBear: p = 2^31 - 2^27 + 1 = 0x78000001, elements in Montgomery form
\ (R = 2^32: a held as aR mod p, in [0, p)).  The reduction needs no
\ general product: -1/p mod 2^32 = 2^31 - 2^27 - 1, and m p = m 2^31 -
\ m 2^27 + m, both shifts and adds.  tom and fromm convert; f+ f- fneg
\ fmul fpow finv work on Montgomery values.
\
\ The extension: x^4 = 11, an element four words in memory (Montgomery,
\ lowest degree first): e4+ e4- e4mul e4inv, given addresses (the result
\ may be either operand).
\
\ Wide integers: n words of 32 bits in memory, least significant first:
\ wzero wcopy wadd wsub wcmp wshl wshr wbits wmul wdivmod, and ud% (a
\ 64-bit value's remainder by a word).  On them, log2x256: tabminer's
\ log2_x256_ceil (miner/src/fri.rs).
\
\ The raw words come from tools/genarith.py through tools/asm2fam.py.
\
\ Not reentrant: e4inv, the shifts, wmul, wdivmod and log2x256 keep state
\ in variables.  um* fmul f+ f- fneg are macros, inlined: a call costs
\ about 40 instructions in fam, a variable's fetch about 60.  So code that
\ makes many products is a raw word that fetches sqt once and keeps it in
\ a7, as e4mul does: there a product and its reduction are 92
\ instructions, straight through.  tabminer's vectors: arith_vectors.fam (made by
\ miner/src/fam_vectors.rs).

:M P 78000001 lit ;
:M ONE FFFFFFE lit ;           \ 1 in Montgomery form: 2^32 mod p
:M R2 45DDDDE3 lit ;           \ 2^64 mod p, to convert in

: sqt variable ;               \ the quarter squares: S[n], n < 2^17
: et1 variable ;  : et2 variable ;  : et3 variable ;   \ e4inv's elements
: lgt variable ;  : lgp variable ;                     \ log2x256's 4 words each

\ ── The product ──

\ sqinit  S[n] = S[n-1] + floor(n/2), from S[0] = 0.
: sqinit
80000 lit alloc sqt !
0 lit dup sqt @ !
20000 lit 1 lit do i 1 lit rshift + dup sqt @ i 2 lit lshift + ! loop drop ;

\ um* ( a b -- lo hi )  a b, 64 bits.  Inline, as the field's words.
:M um* sqt @
83280100 ,   \ lw a7,0(sp)   ( the table )
83254100 ,   \ lw a1,4(sp)   ( b )
